      "writtenOn": "2014-10-24T00:14:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should that one be \u003d 2 since BC1.2 is always lower priority than the type-c resistors?\n\nNot sure why this would be per-board? Isn\u0027t the order set strictly by the standard? (Didn\u0027t see anything in the bug that helped me understand this)",
      "revId": "0ea2c5437f6034a46176fd62382ed467c68d194e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5594aafe_4652c82b",
        "filename": "board/samus_pd/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 47,
      "author": {
        "id": 1103909
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-10-24T00:21:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The problem is if a device has a type-C resistor AND has BC1.2, then we are guaranteed at least the value advertised by the pull-up, but we could get more as given by BC1.2. For example, an Apple charger will show as a 1.5A pull-up, but for BC1.2 it will show up as a 2.4A device. So, we are treating them as the same priority, and the power that is advertised will be a tie break.\n\nThis may not need to be in board directory, but we were imagining that for a given product we might want to prefer a specific charger (like samus might prefer zinger specifically), in which case we would another supplier to this table and give it higher priority.",
      "parentUuid": "35a1f65e_70a8d81d",
      "revId": "0ea2c5437f6034a46176fd62382ed467c68d194e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "75244ea4_108f3c88",
        "filename": "board/samus_pd/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 47,
      "author": {
        "id": 1103909
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-10-24T00:23:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "BTW Mark, since we have you thinking about this, I\u0027m planning to break up BC1.2 into CDP, DCP, SDP, and apple charger. Should we prioritize those or should they all be treated the same priority (default to which will give most power)?",
      "parentUuid": "5594aafe_4652c82b",
      "revId": "0ea2c5437f6034a46176fd62382ed467c68d194e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9592a210_ab65943f",
        "filename": "board/samus_pd/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 47,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001164
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-10-24T01:17:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I guess PD \u003e TypeC \u003e BC1.2 \u003e StdUSB actually says nothing about what to do with proprietary info. But the standard does acknowledge that proprietary can be greater than the TypeC resistor, so we are covered there.\n\nMaybe break BC1.2 into\nPROP2.4A, PROP2.0A, DCP, CDP, PROP1A, SDP0.9A, SDP0.5A, PROP0.5A.\n\nThen for CDP we will hunt for current up to 1.5A and for DCP we can allow the current hunting algorithm to go higher (there are certainly 2A supplies but we could let it get all the way to yoshi\u0027s 3A). Not sure if at this level of the stack we know if USB3 exists to split the SDP.",
      "parentUuid": "75244ea4_108f3c88",
      "revId": "0ea2c5437f6034a46176fd62382ed467c68d194e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
